id: pm-pww8ax
title: "Capability dogfood coverage ratchet: every shipped capability is exercised by real tracked work here, or carries a recorded cover-or-waive disposition"
description: "Measure which shipped, agent-reachable pm capabilities the maintainer workspace actually exercises (custom fields, custom statuses, profiles, calendar types and extension-contributed surfaces are currently at zero), require an adopt/cover/waive disposition for each never-exercised capability, and ratchet the undispositioned set downward so new capabilities cannot ship without one."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: governance,pm-cli,quality-gate,self-hosting
created_at: "2026-07-25T17:49:53.478Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T10:59:30.956Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "A report derived from the runtime schema and contract tables plus workspace history lists every shipped agent-reachable capability with its last-exercised timestamp in this workspace or never; every never-exercised capability carries a recorded disposition of adopt, cover (named scenario test), or waive (documented reason) on its owning item; a gate fails when a capability is neither exercised nor dispositioned, and the undispositioned set is shrinking-only so a newly shipped capability must arrive with its disposition; the currently-zero set (custom fields, custom statuses, applied profiles, Meeting/Event items, extension-contributed types and relationship kinds) is dispositioned as the first pass; the report is token-budgeted and runnable in CI"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: low
confidence: high
